Version: 0.0.2.9000
Date: 2026-09-20
R: 4.4.3
Studies: coverage, power, bench, mclogit, brms
Note: The coverage and power studies were expanded from 11 and 6 cells to 23
 and 13, to cover every model type the package fits rather than only the
 families it started with. New cells: negative binomial; AR(1) and CAR(1) on a
 gaussian response; a censored response; the three accelerated failure time
 families and a frailty Weibull; a Royston-Parmar flexible baseline; a
 dispersion model; a penalised smooth; a random slope. Existing cells are
 unchanged and reproduce the 0.0.1.9000 results.
Note: A replicate counts when the gradient condition holds and the standard
 errors exist, rather than when nlminb reports convergence. Its "false
 convergence (8)" is a stopping heuristic, not a first-order condition: on
 flexible parametric fits a third of replicates reported it while sitting at a
 gradient of 3.7e-03 and recovering the same coefficients as those reporting
 success. The earlier criterion discarded them.
